      "title": "Cardinal Health's CFO Moved $9.9 Million of Stock. Here's What Long-Term Investors Should Know",
      "summary": "Cardinal Health's CFO Aaron Alt sold 42,000 shares worth $9.9 million on August 18, reducing his direct holdings to 20,495 shares. The sale occurred after the stock surged 57% over the past year. Despite the insider sale, the company maintains strong guidance with fiscal 2027 EPS projected at $12.40-$12.60 (13-15% growth), planned capital expenditures of $700 million, and at least $1 billion in share repurchases expected.",
